/-!
# The ATLAS binary matrices for J₄

These are the two matrices of representation `J4G1-f2r112B0` in the online
ATLAS of Finite Group Representations (R. A. Wilson, S. J. Nickerson, J. N. Bray):
https://brauer.maths.qmul.ac.uk/Atlas/v3/matrep/J4G1-f2r112B0

The source lists Type I standard generators of J₄ in dimension 112 over GF(2).
The data below transcribes its text MeatAxe files, retrieved 2026-10-03:
* https://brauer.maths.qmul.ac.uk/Atlas/spor/J4/mtx/J4G1-f2r112B0.m1
* https://brauer.maths.qmul.ac.uk/Atlas/spor/J4/mtx/J4G1-f2r112B0.m2

SHA-256 of the original files (including header and line endings):
* m1: 6320ac1b9801abc409f5ca77ad417da980131003be2cb07d39b2453de3e2c87b
* m2: 4988c24906fabbe00a58a914cfe2d739df26264021d19d9fec168529d64d03f2

Each natural number encodes one row. Bit j is column j, with zero-based
indices; thus the first printed digit of a source row is its least significant
bit here. The 112-digit rows in the source wrap after 80 digits. No transpose,
basis change, or change of generators is applied. The source's field elements
0 and 1 are read as the corresponding elements of `ZMod 2`.

This module defines data only. It makes no assertion that the matrices are
invertible, generate a simple group, or have a particular order.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace Janko4

/-- Matrices in the standard binary representation. -/
abbrev BinaryMatrix := Matrix (Fin 112) (Fin 112) (ZMod 2)

